tional design and communication skills to join our San Francisco office. This is an excellent opportunity to be a part of an award-winning practice that is forward-focused and values the rigorous process of experimentation and implementation. We are equally committed to fostering the professional development of our staff.\n\nOur interior designers play a vital role in shaping experiences from the inside out, bringing material richness, environmental performance, and a human-centered design approach to creating meaningful places where people truly feel they belong. The right candidate will be committed to our mission and core values, bringing compassion and curiosity to their work with a highly collaborative team."}, {"h": "Primary Responsibilities", "t": "Contribute to the interior design process from programming through construction administration, developing design excellence on projects of all sizes and levels of complexity.\nDevelop and articulate compelling design concepts through sketches, presentations, and material palettes that communicate a clear design narrative.\nDevelop selection and specification of finishes, furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FF&E), ensuring integration with architectural design and performance goals.\nCollaborate closely with architects, clients, consultants, and contractors to maintain design intent, quality, and project vision.\nMentor and inspire junior interior design staff, fostering creativity, curiosity, and professional growth.\nConsult with FF&E manufacturers in the research and evaluation of project materials and products.\nCoordinate consultant drawings (extent of responsibility will vary depending upon the characteristics of the project, its size and complexity, its design objectives and specific experience of the team)."}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "Bachelor's or Master's degree in Interior Design or Interior Architecture.\n4-8 years of relevant professional experience, including interior design on complex projects.\nStrong conceptual design skills and a refined sense of materiality and spatial experience.\nExperience with workplace, higher education, cultural, or civic projects preferred.\nProficiency in Revit, Adobe Creative Suite, and rendering tools (Enscape or similar).\nNCIDQ certification and/or professional licensure.\nExcellent communication, collaboration, and organizational skills.\nStrong 3D visualization skills.\nSubstantial knowledge of building materials, product specification, installation and construction methods as they relate to areas of specialty.\nGeneral knowledge of product cost, material vs. install, and building codes in reference but not limited to ADA.\nAbility to anticipate, identify and resolve problems in a timely and positive manner.\nAbility to work effectively within a collaborative team environment."}, {"h": "What We Offer", "t": "EHDD is an award-winning, majority woman-owned firm providing architecture, interiors, planning, and urban design services. We offer competitive benefits, including medical/dental/vision insurance with HSA, transportation benefits, and professional development support.\n\nNotable projects include the AIA Headquarters Renewal, KQED Headquarters, YouTube Campus Expansion, SF Museum of Modern Art, Monterey Bay Aquarium, The Exploratorium, and Goldendale Observatory.\n\nWe are an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply.\n\nApplication Process\n\nSubmit a letter of interest, resume, and portfolio samples. Portfolio must be one PDF attachment, 10-20 pages, maximum 5 MB, illustrating prior relevant work.\n\nApply Now\nwith our quick 3 minute Application!\n* Fields Are Required\n\nWhat is your full name?\n\nFirst Name\n\nHow can we contact you?\n\nEmail\nPhone Number\nNumber Type\nHome\nCell\nWork"}, {"h": "What is your preferred method of communication?", "t": "Email\nText Message\nPlease indicate if you agree to isolved Applicant Tracking's Applicant Communication Policy.\nYes, I agree to be contacted by text messages\nNo, I do not agree to receive text messages\nI agree to isolved Applicant Tracking's Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.*\nApply for this Position\nApply for this Position\nSign Up For Job Alerts!\nName\nEmail\nLocation (city, state or zip code)\nAccept Terms of Service\nI agree to the terms of service and privacy policy.\nSend Me Jobs\n\npowered by Refer.io\n\nShare This Job\nMaintained by isolved People Cloud - © 2026 Refresh\nSearch the FAQ here\nGo\nCommon Job Questions"}], "k": ["ab-testing", "building-codes", "construction-administration", "design-thinking", "enscape", "ffe", "materials", "presentation", "recruiting", "rendering", "revit"]}, "9c808cd9d4": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to Main Content\nHome\nView Your Submissions\nFollow\nInterior Designer | San Francisco\n\nWRNS Studio is seeking an Interior Designer for our San Francisco Studio."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Design and document thoughtful, high-performance interiors across all project phases alongside the design team\nDevelop and craft space plans, schematic design work, FF&E concepts, drawings, models, images, material & mood boards, and detailing aligned with client goals\nCollaborate closely with the design team, consultants, and vendors to ensure project execution\nTranslate strategy, brand, and culture into compelling spatial solutions\nConvey design intent through clear visual storytelling using Revit and rendering tools\nParticipate in design control and documentation of projects in design development, construction document, and supervision phases\nSupport project budgeting, value engineering, sustainability goals, and material selection\nProvide mentorship and direction to junior interior designers and staff, where applicable"}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "Minimum 5+ years of professional experience in Interior Design or Architecture\nProfessional degree in Interior Design or Architecture\nExperience in medium to large-scale projects\nPreferred candidate will have a strong background in workplace interiors and planning\nExpertise in Revit and proficiency in 3D rendering tools such as Enscape, Lumion, or Rhino\nStrong space planning skills and knowledge of systems, furniture, interior finishes and workplace standards\nDemonstrated progressive responsibility in all phases of interior architecture projects\nLeads with curiosity and is a creative problem solver with excellent communication, collaboration, planning and presentation skills\nFamiliarity with sustainable design frameworks, such as LEED, WELL, and Fitwel\nAdobe Creative Suite, SketchUp, AutoCAD, and Bluebeam proficiency preferred\n\nWork location\n\nPlease note, this position is expected to work on-site. WRNS has found that working together and in-person is essential to our collaboration, communication, continuous learning, productivity and innovation."}, {"h": "Salary", "t": "At the time of posting, the salary range for this position is between $85,000 – $110,000 for candidates with 5-10 years of industry experience, $105,000 – $140,000 for candidates with 10-20 years of industry experience, and $135,000 – 165,000 for candidates with 20+ years of industry experience. Our final compensation decisions include a candidate’s experience as well as qualifications, background and education.\n\nApply with\n\nCover Letter\nResume\nPortfolio/Work samples\n\nWe use Submittable to accept and review our submissions.\nContinue\nTechnical Help | Privacy Policy\nPowered by Submittable\n© 2026"}], "k": ["autocad", "bluebeam", "budgeting", "detailing", "enscape", "ffe", "leed", "lumion", "materials", "presentation", "rendering", "revit", "rhino", "sketchup", "space-planning", "sustainability", "writing"]}, "6be3eb9972": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Switch to desktop version\narchitecture\nconstruction\nlandscape\ninteriors\nprefab\nfabrication\nhome goods\nfurniture\nabout\ncontact\nsearch\n."}, {"h": "INTERIOR DESIGNER – LOS ANGELES", "t": "The Interior Designer is responsible for the detailed support of assigned projects and ensures the graceful fulfillment of all related deadlines and design expectations. This role reports to the Interiors Project Manager, Interiors Job Captain, and Interiors Studio Director and supports the overall success and high caliber of projects within the Interiors Studio by contributing excellence in design and production efforts.\n\nThe hiring salary range for this position is $75,000 – $105,000. Any offer of compensation will be determined by a candidate’s education, skills, and experience as assessed during the interview process."}, {"h": "Job Responsibilities", "t": "Perform the daily functions that support a successful project throughout design development, budgeting and procurement, and final installation.\nMeet and communicate directly with consultants and vendors\nClose coordination with architectural, landscape, and construction studios within the Office as required.\nProduce cohesive, accurate, and beautiful furniture plans, interior elevations, interior 3D views, client presentations, and custom furniture drawings as directed\nMeet regularly with Interiors Project Manager and Interiors Job Captain to review project progress and assigned tasks.\nPerform all tasks with diligence, high attention to detail, and according to Interiors Studio and Office standards\n\nRequired Skills\n\nA Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent education in Interior Design at an accredited institution\n2-5 years of relevant industry experience with an exceptional reputation\nVery strong communication, design, and organizational skills\nTechnical skills: Revit, Adobe Creative Suite, Sketchup, Microsoft Excel, Design Manager, Lumion\nThe ability to communicate openly and positively with colleagues and partners at all times\nA positive outlook and strong work ethic\n\nTo apply, please email your cover letter, resume, and work samples (academic and professional) as a single PDF no larger than 5 MB to employment@marmol-radziner.com. No links to portfolios please.\n\nDue to the high volume of resumes we receive, we are only able to respond to those we are interested in interviewing. No telephone calls please.\n\narchitecture\nconstruction\nlandscape\ninteriors\nprefab\nfabrication\nhome goods\nfurniture\nabout\nthe firm\ndesign/build\npeople\ncareers\nawards\npress\ncontact\nsearch"}], "k": ["budgeting", "excel", "lumion", "presentation", "procurement", "revit", "sketchup", "supply-chain"]}, "fdd77701d7": {"s": [{"h": "COOKIE SETTINGS", "t": "We use cookies on our website to give you the most relevant experience by remembering your preferences and repeat visits.\n\nStrictly Necessary\n\nNecessary cookies are absolutely essential for the website to function properly. These cookies ensure basic functionalities and security features of the website, anonymously.\n\nAnalytical or performance\n\nAnalytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc.\n\nFunctionality or appearance\n\nFunctional cookies help to perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collect feedbacks, and other third-party features.\n\nSave Choices\nALL"}, {"h": "COMMERCIAL", "t": "11 & 12 Wellington Place"}, {"h": "COMMERCIAL, RETROFIT", "t": "33 Canada Square\nA lasting legacy: Smithfield Poultry Market\n\nWith"}, {"h": "LUKE REVELEY", "t": "Associate Director"}, {"h": "PLACEMAKING, LIFESTYLE", "t": "Al Jabal Al Aali\n\n15 April 2026\n\nBCO win for Deutsche Bank at 21 Moorfields\n\nReframing the workplace as a seamless, people-first environment.\n\nView More"}, {"h": "BEN CORRIGAN", "t": "Principal Director\n\nView Bio"}, {"h": "WORKPLACE", "t": "BP London"}, {"h": "WORKPLACE", "t": "Capital Group\nCDM Principal Designer Advisor\n\nLocation\n\nLondon\n\nRole\n\nTechnical Group"}, {"h": "Salary", "t": "Competitive\n\nView Role"}, {"h": "CORNELIS VON MOLLENDORFF", "t": "Chief Financial & Operating Officer\n\nView Bio"}, {"h": "CRISTIANO TESTI", "t": "Principal Director\n\nView Bio"}, {"h": "DAVID BLAIR", "t": "Principal Director\n\nView Bio"}], "k": ["networking", "social-media", "sustainability", "training", "urban-design"]}, "2d74a1fb4f": {"s": [{"h": "AVAILABLE POSITIONS", "t": "Experienced Senior Architect / Senior Interior Designer (Copenhagen)\n+10 years of international hospitality experience\n\nExperienced Senior Architect / Senior Interior Designer (Hong Kong)\n+10 years of international hospitality experience\n\nArchitect / Interior Designer (Hong Kong)\n4-5 years of experience\n\nYou are always welcome to send us an unsolicited application, CV and portfolio to jobs@normcph.com. Please note, however, that due to the high number of applications we receive, we’re not be able to respond to each one personally – but we truly appreciate your interest."}, {"h": "WORK", "t": "Architecture\nDesign\nCreative\nVideos"}, {"h": "STUDIO", "t": "About\nPeople\nNewsletter\nContact\nPress"}, {"h": "FOLLOW", "t": "Instagram\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\n\n© 2026 Norm Architects"}], "k": ["social-media"]}, "d09bafa6fe": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to content"}, {"h": "CONTACT", "t": "Senior Interior Designers\n\nWe are growing and looking for talented and experienced Senior Interior Designers to join our London studio and work on a range of different typologies around the world.\n\nAt Conran and Partners, you’ll work across a wide variety of sectors, scales and geographies – from hospitality and residential to commercial – collaborating with our international team of architects and interior designers."}, {"h": "THE ROLE", "t": "We are looking for senior interior designers with proven experience and design sensibilities that sit well with our studio ethos to support new projects in the hospitality, residential and commercial sectors.\n\nThe ideal candidate will have 5+ years of experience with creative drive and technical understanding.\n\nApplicants should have a flair for design and experience working on high-quality projects demonstrated through a beautiful portfolio of work, exhibiting their ability to contribute to the design sensibilities of the practice."}, {"h": "ABOUT YOU", "t": "Minimum 5+ years’ experience working on design-led projects"}, {"h": "Interior design degree or architectural qualifications", "t": "Strong background in the hospitality, high-end residential or workplace sectors\nClient facing with proven experience of job running\nCreative flair, conceptual approach\nUnderstanding of and experience in delivering pitches to drawing packages and schedules\nStrong knowledge and practical experience of AutoCAD or Revit, Sketchup, Rhino and Enscape. 3D rendering abilities.\nStrong graphic communication and presentation skills, InDesign and Photoshop experience is essential.\nExperience leading and managing people, as well as mentoring junior members\nA good knowledge of finishes and FF+E specification along with a desire to continually source new and interesting products.\nExperience working in Asia and fluency in either Mandarin, Cantonese and Japanese is a plus.\n\nThis is a full-time position. All candidates should be eligible to work in the UK.\n\nConran and Partners is an equal opportunities employer and offers the opportunity for growth. We recognise the lack of diversity in our industry, and encourage applicants from under-represented backgrounds to apply. Other benefits include flexible working."}, {"h": "HOW TO APPLY", "t": "Please apply in writing including a CV, portfolio and accompanying letter stating both current and expected salaries to: recruitment@conran.com and clearly mark the subject heading ‘Senior Interior Designer, London’.\n\nPlease note that only successful candidates will be contacted.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you!"}, {"h": "SHARE", "t": "© 2026. All rights reserved. Website design by NexusBond"}], "k": ["autocad", "enscape", "indesign", "photoshop", "presentation", "rendering", "revit", "rhino", "sketchup", "training"]}}